Bayonetta the angel hunting Umbra which  is back for her third installment in the  much beloved Platinum Games title with  the planned release date of October 28  2022 fast approaching here is everything  you need to know about Bayonetta 3.  [Music]  the original Bayonetta was created and  directed by Hideki kamiya the same man  behind Devil May Cry and the Advent of  the arcadey combo heavy 3D action game  style so after creating a 2d game in a  similar style via Beautiful Joe kamiya  created what would become another  beloved combo heavy action game  Bayonetta Bayonetta took with Devil May  Cry started and added a stylistic new  protagonist in its titular character as  well as standout gigantic boss fights  her clothing is her hair which she also  uses for magic and to summon demons and  there's overt sexual overtones  throughout while kamiya created and  directed Bayonetta Bayonetta 2 would be  directed by yusuke Hashimoto with  supervision from kamiya and now  Bayonetta 3 is seeing yet another  director with yusuke Miata taking  control of the project and kamiya  serving as an executive director miata's  past involved designing on various anime  titles and since was credited as a game  designer on the wonderful 101 and astral  chain and level designer on Metal Gear  Solid 5 ground zeros he was also the  lead designer on the now canceled skill  bound and a tweet from scalebound's  former lead producer JP kellems one of  Bayonetta 3's new mechanics controlling  summons is similar to a mechanic from  scale bound JP kellems also mentioned  that he felt yusuke Miata was a super  talented designer so while yusuke Miata  may not be a super recognizable name it  sounds like he has plenty of experience  under his belt as well as a lot of  respect from his peers  speaking on those summons let's talk  about the gameplay like the previous  installments to Bayonetta Bayonetta 3 is  a combo heavy action title what that  means is a heavy focus of the game is on  the combat itself with a score running  throughout while it isn't necessary to  beat any level typically you'll want to  rack up the highest score possible  through Flawless and varied combos while  avoiding damage in order to earn a  higher ranking at the end of each level  this system allows players of a lower  skill to beat a level but also gives a  high skill cap for dedicated players who  want to become the best you'll be able  to play as multiple characters in  Bayonetta 3 who control differently so  let's start with Bayonetta herself  Bayonetta controls mostly like she did  in previous games with each button  corresponding to a different type of  attack like punching kicking or shooting  with her gun boots and doing different  button combinations to pull off combos  dodging is also an important mechanic  not only in avoiding damage but by  pulling off the Dodge at the right time  you'll be able to activate which time or  brief slowdown in time where Bayonetta  can attack enemies as their attack speed  slows through a crawl Bayonetta can also  summon infernal demons to aider in  battle these demons are Ultra powerful  but also quickly drain bayonetta's magic  meter while also leaving her more  vulnerable to attacks meaning you'll  have to strategically bounce back and  forth between using them doing so you  can add to your combo while these  infernal demons were in previous games  they now work as demon slaves allowing  the player to have more direct control  over them Bayonetta also now has a demon  masquerade ability allowing her to fuse  with the summon demon and Grant her  additional abilities these infernal  demons are attached to bayoneta's  various weapons meaning that switching  weapons on the Fly allow allows you to  not only increase bayonet as possible  moveset and combos but also summon more  infernal demons to help with battle some  of these infernal demon abilities go  beyond the battlefield their unique  abilities can also help Bayonetta  explore and find secret Areas when not  in battle with one such example being  Bayonetta masquerading as a spider and  shooting her web to essentially triple  jump and then climb up a wall players  will also be able to control a brand new  character in Viola Viola is a witch in  training who utilizes a sword in Magic  darts while she seems to overall control  mostly like Bayonetta their abilities  differ such as activating which time in  a different way whereas Bayonetta  activates which time while pulling off a  Dodge at the right time Viola activates  which time by countering an enemy's  attack at the correct timing whereas  Bayonetta has multiple demons she can  summon the only one we know of so far  for viola is a giant Cheshire Cat which  is attached to her blade Cheshire Also  may work slightly different and as an  ally rather than a demon slave while  Cheshire is a Channel Viola can't use  her which time and fights with her fists  Bayonetta 3 also includes various  accessibility modes while it includes  the general casual standard and expert  difficulties Bayonetta 3 is also  included The Immortal marionette  accessory players can equip this makes a  so Bayonetta automatically performs  various combos by just tapping one  button the mode is meant to help novice  players but as a caveat does penalize  the player's score on standard mode and  higher Bayonetta 3 also introduces a new  naive Angel mode which conceals some of  the nudity in the game as well as some  of the more graphic enemies  from Bayonetta 3's the witching hour  trailer it seems that Viola is  specifically training under bayonetta's  tutorship the threat this time around  comes from the man-made monkey lie who  serve as this game's major antagonist  and seemed to work for an evil entity  known as the singularity in the Witching  Hour trailer we see Bayonetta seems to  be defeated at some point in time with  Viola needing to take charge however  this could be some sort of fake out  especially as there's different versions  of Bayonetta running around from  different universes so who knows if it's  our Bayonetta Viola's Bayonetta or just  some sort of other fake out entirely  unfortunately I can't talk about  Bayonetta 3 without briefly touching on  the controversy so here we go fans of  the prior Bayonetta games may have  noticed the voice actress for Bayonetta  sounded different as it turns out Helena  Taylor the voice actress of the previous  games was no longer voicing Bayonetta  and had been replaced by seasoned voice  actress Jennifer Hale at the time  according to Miata this was due to  various overlapping circumstances on  October 16th Helena Taylor released a  series of videos on Twitter that blew up  and went viral in these she alleged that  she was only offered four thousand  dollars to voice the entire game it  didn't reflect the living wage for voice  actors and she called for fans of  Bayonetta to boycott Bayonetta 3. Hideki  kamiya responded to this on Twitter  saying sad and deplorable about the  attitude of untruth that's what all I  can tell now by the way beware of my  rules fans were irked in particular by  him saying beware of my rules although  these rules to my understanding are that  he'll block anyone who doesn't message  him in Japanese  on October 18 2022 Bloomberg reported  that Platinum Games had wanted to rehire  Helena Taylor and offered her between  three thousand to four thousand dollars  per four hour recording session not  total with a total of what would come to  around at least fifteen thousand dollars  for roughly 20 hours of work this goes  well above current union rates which  according to sag-aftra are between 900  and 960 dollars per four hour recording  session according to Bloomberg sources  which includes documentation Helena  Taylor then asked for a six-figure sum  plus residuals Platinum turned this down  took on a new actress and then offered  Helena a cameo role for the fee of one  session this story was also corroborated  by video game Chronicle in response  Helena Taylor initially called the  report an absolute lie and a complete  joke then on October 24th she revised  her statement saying she was initially  offered ten thousand dollars negotiated  up for fifteen thousand dollars and  declined deciding that wasn't enough  money still she claims four thousand  dollar dollars per session for five  sessions is a total fabrication on the  side of Bloomberg the report was done by  Jason schreier who's a seasoned games  reporter and has broken plenty of  difficult stories often aimed against  the game industry for mistreatment of  employees and he's regarded as a highly  reputable Source I will say for my part  A game is made by a giant team of  dedicated people who probably had  nothing to do with this situation all  putting years of work into this product  so you can decide what's right for you  based on what we know  Bayonetta 3 releases exclusively to the  Nintendo switch on October 28 2022 and  that wraps up everything you need to  know about Bayonetta 3. I do wonder if  you haven't played a Bayonetta game are  you thinking about hopping on here as  your first one let us know and I'll see  you guys next time
 

